      <title>Five EU states announce plans for immigration ‘return hubs’ in Rwanda</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/16/eu-states-immigration-return-hubs-rwanda</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Germany, Austria, Netherlands, Denmark and Greece likely to face challenges to policy criticised as ‘grave moral failing’&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Five EU member states have announced plans to set up an offshore centre in Rwanda for people with no legal right to stay in Europe, in a pilot scheme that is expected to face legal challenges and has been denounced as “a grave moral failing”.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The five countries – Germany, Austria, the Netherlands, Denmark and Greece – are the first to seek to use the EU’s &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/26/meps-back-plans-for-return-hubs-raising-fears-of-human-rights-black-holes"&gt;newly agreed returns law&lt;/a&gt; that allows&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;people who have exhausted all avenues of appeal against their removal from Europe to be sent to a third country.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/16/eu-states-immigration-return-hubs-rwanda"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
